//? Title: SSS* through memory search: actual probes and explicit preprocessing
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
This implementation uses an upper-bound MTD driver around alpha-beta with
transposition memory. Actual null-window probes and bound writes expose how the
root interval closes. Complete-tree validation reads every leaf, so
preprocessing and search work are reported separately.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Begin with a finite upper guess from the validated leaves. Each root query uses
adjacent window endpoints separated by the supplied value resolution; fail-low
tightens the upper bound and fail-high raises the lower bound. Reuse lower/upper
transposition bounds keyed by actual node identities. Stop when the driver
bounds meet, or explicitly return unresolved on probe exhaustion. Resolution
must not exceed the smallest distinct finite leaf gap. Floating adjacent
endpoints use nextafter when ordinary addition/subtraction cannot move a bound.
Classical SSS* dominance results concern specified ordered-tree query models;
they do not prove lower total work for this validating implementation or
arbitrary alpha-beta variants.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sss_star_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/sss_star.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto tree = a::sss_example_tree(2, 17);
    auto r = a::sss_star_trace(tree, true);
    std::print("| actual probe | alpha | beta | value | driver lower | driver upper | search leaf reads " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.history)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.index, s.alpha,
                   s.beta, s.value, s.lower, s.upper, s.search_leaf_reads);
    std::print("Converged {}; preflight leaf reads {}; actual bound writes {}.\n",
               r.converged, r.preflight_leaf_reads, r.bounds.size());
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0},
                         std::format("{} validated leaves",
                                     r.preflight_leaf_reads));
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual null-window probes", r.probes));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Root value {}; closed {}", r.result.value,
                                     r.converged));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/sss_star_tiny.svg");
}
```
