> API and interpretation

Leaf flags, children, finite values, resolution and depth are checked before
search. Zero probe cap returns an unresolved interval; the legacy value-only
wrapper throws on unresolved exhaustion. Returned best_child remains-1 because
no extra principal-variation extraction is performed. Search counters exclude
the separately disclosed full validation/bound-initialization scan. Histories
own node IDs rather than pointers.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- Stockman, A Minimax Algorithm Better Than Alpha-Beta?, Artificial
  Intelligence12 (1979),179-196
- Plaat et al., Best-First Fixed-Depth Minimax Algorithms, Artificial
  Intelligence87 (1996),255-293

